Keyframe Studio contains no Spine runtime code. Its engine (src/engine) is written from the Spine
4.2 JSON format's documented semantics and is checked against the official runtime by comparing
outputs only.

The optional Spine add-on downloads Esoteric Software's official spine-player package
(@esotericsoftware/spine-player, pinned version and integrity in src/core/spine-addon.js) into
the user's app data, and only after the user accepts the Spine Runtimes License
(https://esotericsoftware.com/spine-runtimes-license), which requires each user to hold their own
Spine Editor license. That runtime is Esoteric Software's and is not covered by Keyframe Studio's
license.

Asset library (assets/library): each pack records its license, author and source in its
pack.json, and is taken only under CC0, MIT or CC BY. Packs whose license asks for credit:
- assets/library/keyframe-basics: "Keyframe basics" by The Keyframe Studio contributors, MIT
  (https://github.com/Zeatrex01/keyframe).

